        "severity": "soft",
        "claim": "expectedRegion()'s active-nav aria-current regex inserts the attribute before a self-closing tag's trailing `/>` instead of before `>`, producing malformed markup for any data-nav element written in self-closing form",
        "file": "spec/scripts/lib/shell-region.js",
        "line": 170,
        "impact": "If a shell canon's nav item is ever authored as a self-closing tag, sync/adopt would write broken HTML into every mock instead of well-formed markup",
        "evidence": "Executed repro: expectedRegion('<div data-shell-canon=\"app2\" class=\"shell\"><nav data-slot=\"nav\" data-contract=\"none\"><a data-nav=\"x\" href=\"#\"/></nav><main data-slot=\"content\"></main></div>', 'app2', 'CONTENT', 'x') returned '<a data-nav=\"x\" href=\"#\"/ aria-current=\"page\"></nav>' — the `/` lands mid-attribute rather than closing the tag. Not exercised by any spec fixture or AC (the D1 contract's nav items are always `<a>...</a>`, never self-closed, and self-closing a non-void element is not valid HTML to begin with), so this is advisory rather than a defect in the shipped behavior."
      }
    ],
